c Graph H_3 of Theorem 1 in 'The CLIQUES Algorithm Is Not Output-Polynomial' (Sec. 3)
c target n = 50; nearest H_k has n = 2k^2+9k = 45 vertices (k = 3)
c maximal cliques: 145 (Lemma bound (k+1)(2k(k+3)+1) = 148 <= n^2 = 2025)
c every run of CLIQUES makes at least 2^(k+1)-1 = 15 recursive calls (one run with min-label tie-breaking and increasing order: 363)
c vertices: guards g_i = 1..3; core a_i = k+2i-1, b_i = k+2i (4..9); witnesses 10..45, 6 per core vertex in the order a_1, b_1, a_2, ...
p edge 45 315
